# Data NEVER enters the repo. The challenge supplies it; redistribution is not ours to do.
# Two exceptions, both code or fitted parameters, never records: the stored ADS-B stack models (fitted models; 7.4 MB) that
# every final config reads and a clone cannot regenerate (docs/fm1/DATA_SOURCES.md), and the Rome E2 rules file
# (data/rome_hunt_2026_09_23/agent_E_rules.py, force-added). Git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so
# the stack models' path is opened one level at a time.
data/*
!data/r12/
data/r12/*
!data/r12/r13_stack_full/
data/r12/r13_stack_full/*
!data/r12/r13_stack_full/models_lgbcat/
*.parquet
*.csv
*.zip

# Outputs: submission files are regenerable (docs/fm1/REPRODUCE.md).
submissions/
*.joblib
*.pkl

# The development record (registrations, ledgers, analysis reports) is not part of the repository: it is not needed
# to run, test or rebuild FM1, and docs/fm1/ describes what it established (README.md, "Repository layout").
plans/
reports/

# Run logs and fitted model artefacts: regenerable (docs/fm1/REPRODUCE.md), never part of the record.
logs/
artifacts/

# Handoffs are working files for the next session, never part of the record.
_HANDOFF_*.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Credentials — nothing with a secret ever gets tracked
.env
*.pem
credentials*
*_secret*
